      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Rate limiter wait (mean), by channel",
      "description": "How long a message waits for its channel's rate on average: about 10 ms at 100 a second while a burst queues up. The mean, rather than a percentile, is exact here: the histogram's buckets (10 ms, 25 ms) are too coarse for a percentile near 10 ms.",
